<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology/v2> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "g911"@en .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "An OWL 2 ontology that models clothing items, their attributes (color, material, size, formality), and outfit-level compatibility relations. The ontology is designed to support a rule-based outfit combination engine that recommends harmonious outfits based on color theory, material compatibility, occasion, season, and personalized user preferences."@en .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-04-01"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-05-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Clothing Ontology for Outfit Combination Engine"@en .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "clo" .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-o/" .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Version 2 extends v1 with: an Outfit module (Outfit class and part-of properties), a richer Attribute module (ColorScheme, ColorUndertone, FormalityLevel), a User module for personalization, schema.org alignment, and one machine-readable SWRL rule plus documented rule designs for color-harmony, formality-consistency, season-coherence and material-conflict heuristics."@en .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#priorVersion> <http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology/v1> .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/g911/ontologies/2026/3/Clothing-Ontology> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "2.0" .
